# Build context hygiene. Everything here either does not belong in an image, or
# would silently make the build non-reproducible by shipping a machine's local
# state into it.

# SECRETS. `.env` holds JWT_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM, RESET_CODE_PEPPER and the Firebase
# service account JSON. It must never enter a build context: every COPY layer is
# readable by anyone who can pull the image, and `docker history` shows it even
# if a later layer deletes the file. `.env.example` is the documented shape and
# is safe, so it is NOT excluded.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# A local virtualenv is built for this machine's OS and CPU. Copying it in would
# shadow the interpreter's own site-packages with Windows binaries inside a
# Linux image -- a failure that surfaces at import time, far from its cause.
.venv/
venv/

# Tool caches: large, machine-specific, and regenerated on demand.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.log

# Version control and editor state.
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
